# authorized.txt — list of accounts allowed on this system.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Copy this file to "authorized.txt" (next to harden.sh), or pass a path
#      with --authorized /path/to/file.
#   2. Replace the example names below with the REAL authorized accounts taken
#      from your competition README / system documentation.
#   3. Run:  sudo ./harden.sh   and choose the "User & Group Audit" section.
#
# RULES:
#   * Lines starting with '#' are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
#   * Inline comments after a value are allowed (everything after '#' is dropped).
#   * Two sections, introduced exactly by [users] and [sudoers]:
#       [users]   = EVERY human login account that is allowed to exist.
#       [sudoers] = the subset of those users allowed admin (sudo/wheel) access.
#   * Any human account (UID >= 1000) NOT under [users] is flagged for deletion.
#   * Any sudo/wheel member NOT under [sudoers] is flagged for removal from that
#     group (the account itself is kept).
#   * The account currently running the script is never offered for deletion.
#   * 'root' is handled automatically and does not need to be listed.

[users]
alice
bob
charlie

[sudoers]
alice
bob
